TOKEN tinybird_ingest APPEND
TOKEN tinybird_read READ

DESCRIPTION >
Every production D1 call from Gen and Enter, kept 3 days, to attribute D1
stalls to the query shapes and routes running in the seconds before them.
`sql` holds the statement text with placeholders only (batches joined by
";\n"); `error_code` is empty for a successful call.

SCHEMA >
`timestamp`       DateTime64(3)          `json:$.timestamp`,
`service`         LowCardinality(String) `json:$.service`,
`environment`     LowCardinality(String) `json:$.environment` DEFAULT 'undefined',
`route_path`      LowCardinality(String) `json:$.route_path` DEFAULT '',
`method`          LowCardinality(String) `json:$.method` DEFAULT '',
`request_id`      String                 `json:$.request_id` DEFAULT '',
`edge_colo`       LowCardinality(String) `json:$.edge_colo` DEFAULT '',
`duration_ms`     UInt32                 `json:$.duration_ms`,
`sql_duration_ms` Nullable(Float32)      `json:$.sql_duration_ms`,
`rows_read`       Nullable(UInt32)       `json:$.rows_read`,
`rows_written`    Nullable(UInt32)       `json:$.rows_written`,
`statements`      UInt16                 `json:$.statements` DEFAULT 1,
`error_code`      LowCardinality(String) `json:$.error_code` DEFAULT '',
`sql`             String                 `json:$.sql` DEFAULT ''

ENGINE "MergeTree"
ENGINE_PARTITION_KEY "toDate(timestamp)"
ENGINE_SORTING_KEY "environment, timestamp"
ENGINE_TTL "toDateTime(timestamp) + toIntervalDay(3)"
